ly; discoverValidationModulesIn takes the\n752:// isAndroidModule reads and writes the filesystem directly; isAndroidModuleIn takes the\n760:// reason in the structured result (spec pose-structured-validation-results).\n922:\t\t\t// A check's output is captured by default; --verbose streams it\n923:\t\t\t// (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R7).\n961:\t\t\t\t// pose-cli-output-machine-channel, R2).\n993:\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: result output paths must remain inside the project.\", \"Erro: paths de saída de resultado devem permanecer dentro do projeto.\"))\n1001:\t// The report --report writes records this run, so it reads this run's own\n1002:\t// output. It used to look for a pose-validate.latest.log that native\n1003:\t// validation never writes, and every report said \"Fill manually\" and \"No\n1004:\t// validation output detected\" under an outcome it could not support (spec\n1007:\t// from its printed output (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R5).\n1244:\t// Checks run up to jobs at a time; results are shown and counted here,\n1246:\t// pose-validate-concurrent-steps R1). --verbose streams a check's output,\n1385:\tfor name, writer := range map[string]struct {\n1387:\t\twrite func(string, validationRunResult) error\n1389:\t\t\"json\":  {jsonOut, writeValidationJSON},\n1390:\t\t\"junit\": {junitOut, writeValidationJUnit},\n1391:\t\t\"sarif\": {sarifOut, writeValidationSARIF},\n1393:\t\tif writer.path == \"\" {\n1396:\t\ttarget := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(writer.path))\n1397:\t\tif name == \"json\" && canonicalResultsPath != \"\" && normalizeValidationOutputPath(writer.path) == canonicalResultsPath {\n1398:\t\t\terr := publishCanonicalValidationJSONIn(store, writer.path, canonicalResultsPath, run)\n1417:\t\tif err := writer.write(target, run); err != nil {\n1443:\t\tif err := writeExecutionPlan(target, plan); err != nil {\n1466:// the structured replacement for parsing the printed output (spec\n1467:// pose-cli-o